    <section class="story rise" id="story" aria-label="How NERO began">
      <div><p class="kicker">About NERO</p><h1 class="big">How NERO began</h1></div>
      <div class="body"><p>A beautiful chair can look ordinary in the wrong light. NERO began with that thought.</p>
        <p>Italian furniture houses have had decades to earn their names. NERO had none. So instead of borrowing a past, it set one rule it could keep from the first day: every piece is designed together with the light that shows it best.</p>
        <p>Each collection ships with its own lamp. Each piece arrives with a note on where the lamp goes and where the shadow falls. The colours come from rooms in late afternoon, and the lineage is Italian modernism, the work of Gio Ponti and Carlo Scarpa, carried into rooms in Kigali and beyond.</p>
        <p>The brief was simple to write and hard to meet: make a new house feel inherited.</p></div>
    </section>
